⚡🇱🇧🇮🇱 Emergency teams and local firefighters in Harouf, southern Lebanon, are struggling to contain a series of intense fires spreading across multiple neighborhoods. Urgent calls have been issued to owners of private water tankers to head to the area immediately to support emergency responders.

Harouf has been hit by an unusually high frequency of fires. The  emergency originated from a mix of reasons, eye witness reports that several of the blazes were reportedly triggered by quad copters strikes , while others erupted after residents burning trash lost control of the flames, allowing them to spread rapidly through dry brush.

